1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:07,259
In twenty sixteen, at a press conference in Iraq, the country's transport minister made an astonishing claim.

2
00:00:07,259 --> 00:00:15,266
Five thousand years ago, he said, the Sumerians built an airport in the south of his country, and launched spaceships from it.

3
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:18,081
His source was not an excavation.

4
00:00:18,081 --> 00:00:28,899
It was a book from nineteen seventy-six, which says that beings called the Anunnaki came down from a hidden planet, mined gold on Earth, and created us.

5
00:00:29,366 --> 00:00:31,370
The name Anunnaki is real.

6
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:37,843
It appears on clay again and again, across two thousand years of Mesopotamian texts.

7
00:00:37,843 --> 00:00:42,466
The question is what the people who wrote it actually meant.

8
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:45,860
So tonight we read that one word three ways.

9
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,723
Reading one: they were gods.

10
00:00:47,723 --> 00:00:50,983
Reading two: they were kings, remembered as gods.

11
00:00:50,983 --> 00:00:53,977
Reading three: they were visitors from space.

12
00:00:53,977 --> 00:00:56,971
Each reading gets tested against the tablets.

13
00:00:56,971 --> 00:00:59,100
Then a scorecard, and a verdict.

14
00:01:03,566 --> 00:01:06,175
First, how do we know anything at all?

15
00:01:06,175 --> 00:01:11,118
Writing began here, in southern Iraq, more than five thousand years ago.

16
00:01:11,118 --> 00:01:16,266
Early cities like Uruk kept their accounts by pressing marks into wet clay.

17
00:01:16,733 --> 00:01:17,701
Clay survives.

18
00:01:17,701 --> 00:01:23,924
Between half a million and two million cuneiform tablets have been dug up in modern times.

19
00:01:23,924 --> 00:01:29,733
Only a fraction, perhaps thirty to a hundred thousand, have been read and published.

20
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,277
For two thousand years nobody could read them.

21
00:01:33,277 --> 00:01:39,966
Scholars rebuilt the script in the nineteenth century, and today a myth can be checked line by line.

22
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:42,601
One sign matters for our case.

23
00:01:42,601 --> 00:01:44,119
It looks like a star.

24
00:01:44,119 --> 00:01:46,649
On its own it means sky, or heaven.

25
00:01:46,649 --> 00:01:51,998
Written before a name, it is silent, and simply marks that name as divine.

26
00:01:51,998 --> 00:01:53,733
Scholars call it dingir.

27
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,472
Remember that star.

28
00:01:55,472 --> 00:02:01,500
It returns in all three readings, because the argument turns on who is allowed to wear it.

29
00:02:01,966 --> 00:02:03,999
Reading one is the plainest.

30
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:09,660
In Sumerian the name is written a-nun-na, probably meaning princely offspring.

31
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:14,233
The Anunna were the children of An, the sky, and Ki, the earth.

32
00:02:14,699 --> 00:02:26,466
The earliest known uses of the word come from inscriptions of Gudea, ruler of Lagash, around twenty one hundred BC, and from the Third Dynasty of Ur.

33
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:37,888
In the oldest texts they are the great gods themselves, probably the seven who decree: An, Enlil, Enki, Ninhursag, Nanna, Utu and Inanna.

34
00:02:37,888 --> 00:02:42,766
Their job, the poems say, was to decree the fates of mankind.

35
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:46,892
But the tablets never agree on how many there were.

36
00:02:46,892 --> 00:02:50,551
One text links fifty Anunnaki to the city of Eridu.

37
00:02:50,551 --> 00:02:56,147
In Inanna's Descent there are just seven, sitting as judges in the underworld.

38
00:02:56,147 --> 00:03:01,599
A late Babylonian epic counts three hundred in heaven and six hundred below.

39
00:03:02,066 --> 00:03:08,825
No complete list of their names has ever been found, and no temple or picture of them as a group.

40
00:03:08,825 --> 00:03:12,099
As a team, they live almost only in literature.

41
00:03:12,566 --> 00:03:22,040
Mesopotamians pictured a god as a giant in human form, wrapped in a terrifying radiance, living in its temple, inside its statue.

42
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:25,933
Priests dressed that statue, and set meals before it.

43
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:29,712
The gods even had vehicles: barges and chariots.

44
00:03:29,712 --> 00:03:36,199
They carried the statues to festivals, and sometimes to a battlefield, so the god could watch.

45
00:03:36,666 --> 00:03:42,453
Now the most important tablet of all, because the visitor theory is built on it.

46
00:03:42,453 --> 00:03:48,096
The Babylonian epic of Atrahasis opens: when the gods, like men, did the work.

47
00:03:48,096 --> 00:03:53,666
Junior gods, the Igigi, dig the rivers and canals while the senior gods rule.

48
00:03:54,133 --> 00:03:55,420
The workers revolt.

49
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:59,555
At night they surround the house of Enlil, chief of the gods.

50
00:03:59,555 --> 00:04:06,400
To end the strike, the gods decide to make a substitute: a creature that will carry the load instead.

51
00:04:06,866 --> 00:04:14,756
Enki and the mother goddess Mami take clay, mix it with the blood of a slain god, and shape the first humans.

52
00:04:14,756 --> 00:04:17,217
Mami hands them a carrying basket.

53
00:04:17,217 --> 00:04:19,099
Humanity is born as labor.

54
00:04:19,566 --> 00:04:24,055
Then humans multiply, and their noise keeps the gods awake.

55
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:26,869
Plague, drought, and finally a flood.

56
00:04:26,869 --> 00:04:31,966
Enki warns one wise man, Atrahasis, who builds a boat and survives.

57
00:04:32,433 --> 00:04:35,287
And here is the detail that matters most.

58
00:04:35,287 --> 00:04:41,065
During the flood, with no humans left to feed them, the gods go hungry and thirsty.

59
00:04:41,065 --> 00:04:45,800
When Atrahasis makes his offering, they gather around it like flies.

60
00:04:46,266 --> 00:04:48,744
Over time the word even drifts.

61
00:04:48,744 --> 00:04:55,699
Later, Anunnaki usually means the gods of the underworld, and Igigi the gods of heaven.

62
00:04:56,166 --> 00:04:57,963
Finding for reading one.

63
00:04:57,963 --> 00:05:03,876
In the tablets, the Anunnaki are gods: immortal, quarrelsome, fed by sacrifice.

64
00:05:03,876 --> 00:05:06,196
That is not our interpretation.

65
00:05:06,196 --> 00:05:08,666
It is how the scribes wrote them.

66
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:11,943
Reading two is older than it sounds.

67
00:05:11,943 --> 00:05:21,467
Around three hundred BC the Greek writer Euhemerus argued that gods were simply famous rulers, remembered and exaggerated.

68
00:05:21,467 --> 00:05:24,199
Maybe the Anunnaki were real kings.

69
00:05:24,666 --> 00:05:29,116
The star witness for this reading is the Sumerian King List.

70
00:05:29,116 --> 00:05:35,866
Its best-known copy, the Weld-Blundell prism, dates to the reign of King Sin-magir of Isin.

71
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:41,834
It opens: after the kingship descended from heaven, the kingship was in Eridu.

72
00:05:41,834 --> 00:05:44,866
Kingship literally comes down from the sky.

73
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:47,999
Then come eight kings before the flood.

74
00:05:47,999 --> 00:05:52,579
The first, Alulim, rules twenty-eight thousand eight hundred years.

75
00:05:52,579 --> 00:05:57,295
Together they reign two hundred forty-one thousand two hundred years.

76
00:05:57,295 --> 00:06:00,166
One of them, Dumuzid, is a well-known god.

77
00:06:00,633 --> 00:06:07,846
After the flood, kingship descends again, to Kish, and the reigns start to shrink, from centuries to decades.

78
00:06:07,846 --> 00:06:09,633
Legend fading into history.

79
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:15,068
Alien fans love one entry: Etana, the king who ascended to heaven.

80
00:06:15,068 --> 00:06:21,466
In his own myth he flies there on the back of an eagle, a story, not a flight report.

81
00:06:21,933 --> 00:06:30,813
And then a name everyone knows: Gilgamesh of Uruk, given one hundred twenty-six years, and a father described as a phantom.

82
00:06:30,813 --> 00:06:39,333
Most historians think a real Gilgamesh ruled Uruk early in the third millennium BC, and was later worshipped as a god.

83
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,954
But historians read the King List as politics.

84
00:06:42,954 --> 00:06:50,566
Each dynasty edited it to show that kingship had always passed to one city at a time, and now belonged to them.

85
00:06:51,033 --> 00:06:52,844
Then the evidence turns.

86
00:06:52,844 --> 00:07:01,449
Around twenty two hundred fifty BC, Naram-Sin of Akkad became the first Mesopotamian king known to claim divinity.

87
00:07:01,449 --> 00:07:08,166
On his victory stele he climbs a mountain wearing a horned helmet, the headgear of a god.

88
00:07:08,633 --> 00:07:13,437
A statue base found in nineteen seventy-four, at Bassetki, says why.

89
00:07:13,437 --> 00:07:23,399
After he crushed a great revolt, the citizens asked the great gods that Naram-Sin be made the god of their city, and they built him a temple.

90
00:07:23,866 --> 00:07:28,993
From then on his name is written with the star of divinity in front of it.

91
00:07:28,993 --> 00:07:35,366
Later, Shulgi of Ur did the same, and the kings of Ur called Gilgamesh their divine brother.

92
00:07:35,833 --> 00:07:37,639
Finding for reading two.

93
00:07:37,639 --> 00:07:40,197
Some kings really did become gods.

94
00:07:40,197 --> 00:07:44,787
But they climbed into a divine category that already existed.

95
00:07:44,787 --> 00:07:48,699
The great gods are never presented as retired kings.

96
00:07:49,166 --> 00:07:52,366
Reading three is the one most people have heard.

97
00:07:52,366 --> 00:07:57,100
In nineteen seventy-six, Zecharia Sitchin published The Twelfth Planet.

98
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:02,100
His books have sold millions of copies, in more than twenty-five languages.

99
00:08:02,566 --> 00:08:10,966
Sitchin, born in Baku, was a journalist and then a shipping executive in New York, who taught himself to read cuneiform.

100
00:08:11,433 --> 00:08:23,033
He built on Erich von Däniken's Chariots of the Gods, from nineteen sixty-eight, which read Sumerian texts as alien contact, and turned it into a full history.

101
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:34,700
His claim: beyond Neptune hides a planet called Nibiru, on a long elliptical orbit that brings it into the inner solar system every three thousand six hundred years.

102
00:08:35,166 --> 00:08:44,433
Its people, the Anunnaki, landed on Earth about four hundred fifty thousand years ago looking for gold, and mined it in Africa.

103
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:53,929
When the miners rebelled against the work, Enki proposed a worker made by crossing their genes with those of Homo erectus.

104
00:08:53,929 --> 00:08:58,666
Humanity, says Sitchin, was a slave species built for the mines.

105
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:00,411
Notice what he did.

106
00:09:00,411 --> 00:09:03,438
That is the Atrahasis story from reading one.

107
00:09:03,438 --> 00:09:08,415
Sitchin kept the plot, and swapped clay and blood for genetic engineering.

108
00:09:08,415 --> 00:09:14,133
It is his strongest card, because the myth really does say humans were made as labor.

109
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,736
He went further.

110
00:09:15,736 --> 00:09:26,533
The evil wind in the Lament for Ur, he wrote, was fallout from nuclear weapons, used in a war between alien factions, in the year twenty twenty-four BC.

111
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,241
Nibiru then escaped the books.

112
00:09:29,241 --> 00:09:37,088
Doomsday websites predicted its arrival in two thousand three, then twenty twelve, then twenty seventeen.

113
00:09:37,088 --> 00:09:40,899
NASA's answer never changed: Nibiru does not exist.

114
00:09:41,366 --> 00:09:43,781
Ancient astronaut fans add pictures.

115
00:09:43,781 --> 00:09:51,899
Assyrian palace reliefs show winged figures carrying what looks like a handbag, and wearing what looks like a wristwatch.

116
00:09:52,366 --> 00:10:01,610
And a cylinder seal in Berlin, catalogue number VA two forty-three, which Sitchin read as the Sun circled by eleven planets.

117
00:10:01,610 --> 00:10:04,666
Twelve bodies in all: the twelfth planet.

118
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:06,033
Now the test.

119
00:10:06,033 --> 00:10:13,302
We check Sitchin the way any translation is checked: against dictionaries, other copies, and specialists.

120
00:10:13,302 --> 00:10:14,133
Five claims.

121
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,914
Claim one: Nibiru.

122
00:10:15,914 --> 00:10:19,859
In Akkadian, nibiru means crossing, a ford or a ferry.

123
00:10:19,859 --> 00:10:28,478
In the creation epic, Nibiru is Marduk's star, which he made visible in heaven to mark the turning point of the stars.

124
00:10:28,478 --> 00:10:31,399
Babylonian astronomy ties it to Jupiter.

125
00:10:31,866 --> 00:10:34,124
The orbit also fails on physics.

126
00:10:34,124 --> 00:10:39,274
A planet on that path would not keep the same period for even two passes.

127
00:10:39,274 --> 00:10:42,166
And a body that big would be easy to see.

128
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:44,601
Claim two: twelve planets.

129
00:10:44,601 --> 00:10:54,289
The catalogued cuneiform astronomy texts, from the MUL-APIN compendium on, know five planets, the ones visible to the naked eye.

130
00:10:54,289 --> 00:10:56,333
Not one tablet counts more.

131
00:10:56,799 --> 00:10:58,468
Claim three: the seal.

132
00:10:58,468 --> 00:11:05,446
Its lines of writing, which Sitchin did not discuss, read: Dubsiga, Ili-illat, your servant.

133
00:11:05,446 --> 00:11:07,798
A name, an owner, a dedication.

134
00:11:07,798 --> 00:11:09,466
Nothing about planets.

135
00:11:09,933 --> 00:11:12,901
And the central symbol is not the Sun.

136
00:11:12,901 --> 00:11:16,729
The Sun god's disk has wavy rays inside a circle.

137
00:11:16,729 --> 00:11:22,899
This is a star, the usual marker of a god, and dots are how artists drew stars.

138
00:11:23,366 --> 00:11:25,027
Claim four: the words.

139
00:11:25,027 --> 00:11:30,161
Sitchin said the sign dingir meant pure ones of the blazing rockets.

140
00:11:30,161 --> 00:11:33,105
The sign is a star, meaning sky or god.

141
00:11:33,105 --> 00:11:39,899
Historians who checked his references found quotations cut short and taken out of context.

142
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:42,074
Claim five: the handbag.

143
00:11:42,074 --> 00:11:45,418
The museums that hold these reliefs explain it.

144
00:11:45,418 --> 00:11:51,537
The bucket held holy water, and the cone, called in Akkadian a purifier, sprinkled it.

145
00:11:51,537 --> 00:11:56,233
The wristwatch is a bracelet with a rosette, a symbol of divinity.

146
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:57,801
One last check.

147
00:11:57,801 --> 00:12:06,613
In Atrahasis, people are made of clay and divine blood, not genes, and their makers nearly starve without our offerings.

148
00:12:06,613 --> 00:12:09,990
Starfaring engineers who need us to feed them?

149
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:11,899
The tablet describes gods.

150
00:12:12,366 --> 00:12:13,131
Case closed.

151
00:12:13,131 --> 00:12:14,533
Here is the scorecard.

152
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,482
The Anunnaki appear in real texts: evidence.

153
00:12:18,482 --> 00:12:21,568
In those texts they are gods: evidence.

154
00:12:21,568 --> 00:12:25,684
Some kings became gods: evidence, from Naram-Sin on.

155
00:12:25,684 --> 00:12:29,166
The great gods were once kings: no evidence.

156
00:12:29,633 --> 00:12:34,216
Nibiru is a hidden planet: debunked, it is Marduk's star.

157
00:12:34,216 --> 00:12:38,799
Seal VA two forty-three shows the solar system: debunked.

158
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:42,899
The Anunnaki were visitors from space: no evidence.

159
00:12:43,366 --> 00:12:44,241
The verdict.

160
00:12:44,241 --> 00:12:45,481
Reading one wins.

161
00:12:45,481 --> 00:12:53,866
The Anunnaki were gods: the princely children of the sky, who decreed fates, judged the dead, and needed to be fed.

162
00:12:54,333 --> 00:12:56,912
Reading two survives as a footnote.

163
00:12:56,912 --> 00:13:01,922
Kings like Naram-Sin and Shulgi reached up for the star of divinity.

164
00:13:01,922 --> 00:13:04,133
But the gods were there first.

165
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:08,781
Reading three is a modern story written over an ancient one.

166
00:13:08,781 --> 00:13:18,399
It took a real myth about labor and rebellion, and replaced clay with DNA, a star with a planet, and a servant's seal with a map of space.

167
00:13:18,866 --> 00:13:27,520
The real tablets are stranger, and better: gods on strike, kings who became gods, and the first humans, handed a basket.

168
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:30,333
Anyone can read them now, line by line.

169
00:13:30,799 --> 00:13:31,952
That is the case.

170
00:13:31,952 --> 00:13:35,613
Gods, kings, or visitors: which reading convinced you?

171
00:13:35,613 --> 00:13:40,833
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery on trial.
